Today is Monday morning.
My colleague Rohan and I are in the office.
Our manager, Suresh, calls us to his desk.
We go near his desk.
"Good morning, Suresh," I say to him.
Suresh smiles and says, "Good morning."
"Sit."
"We have received a new software project," he says.
"Maya, welcome to this new core team."
"Thank you, Suresh," I say happily.
Suresh gives us information about the project.
"The client has requested a new system from us," he explains.
"They have specified some important things."
Rohan asks, "Is this project very big?"
Suresh nods and says, "Yes, this work is big."
I open my notebook.
Suresh tells us all the client's demands.
I write down all those demands in the notebook.
I am a software engineer.
I have done such work before, so I am ready.
I am very excited for this new work.
